{
  "$comment": [
    "The macro API's surface: every key of game.drpg (scripts/api.mjs DrpgApi, through normalise) with its kind, as typeof answers it ('array' and 'null' apart). Tier 0 R1560 holds the live object to this file, through tests-kit.mjs apiSurfaceProblems (E52 C6; S17-51, E52-21; D25 as E52 reads it: a key leaves game.drpg only after at least one release as an alias). suiteRolling, the switch the test runner (scripts/tests.mjs) sets on game.drpg while a run lasts, is not a key of the surface.",
    "ADD a key: put it on DrpgApi and its row in keys.",
    "RENAME a key old to new (E66 does this): put new on DrpgApi and in keys; keep old on DrpgApi beside it ('old: theNewFunction' or the older function), and move old's row from keys to aliases as { target: 'new', since: '<the stage id, as tools/stages.json has it, or a release>', keepUntil: '<the first release old may leave, past since's release>' or null for no end set, note }.",
    "REMOVE an alias once module.json's version has reached its keepUntil: take it off DrpgApi and move its row, unchanged, from aliases to removed. A key does not go straight from keys to removed.",
    "R1560 fails: a live key in neither keys nor aliases; a key of keys gone from game.drpg; a kind that differs; an alias gone from game.drpg and not in removed, or whose target is no key of keys; a since that is no stage and no release; a keepUntil not past since's release; a removal before its keepUntil; two live keys holding one function where neither is the other's alias.",
    "notes: what a key answers where the code is about to change (R1561 holds them to config.mjs and eclipse.mjs)."
  ],
